Servers older than 5.5 (no CLIENT_PLUGIN_AUTH) get an empty password: the
handshake scramble is tagged caching_sha2_password while the client picks
mysql_native_password, so the scramble is discarded and an empty auth
response is sent ("Access denied ... (using password: NO)").

Backport of upstream 8.3/8.4 commit:
https://github.com/mysql/mysql-server/commit/56b9aaede424d766649382d38fb6a0de3d4e702f
Bug#36066161: 8.3 client unable authenticate into to 5.0.15 server with
mysql_native_password

--- a/sql-common/client.cc	2026-10-09 12:22:37.969490343 +0200
+++ b/sql-common/client.cc	2026-10-09 12:22:37.979490343 +0200
@@ -6921,7 +6921,7 @@
       }
     } else {
       ctx->scramble_data_len = (int)(pkt_end - ctx->scramble_data);
-      ctx->scramble_plugin = caching_sha2_password_plugin_name;
+      ctx->scramble_plugin = native_password_plugin_name;
     }
   } else {
     set_mysql_error(mysql, CR_MALFORMED_PACKET, unknown_sqlstate);
